        "ImageDescription": {
          "value": "<p>A plate lunch from the Ward Farmer's Market: <b>ahi poke</b> (raw ahi tuna marinated in shoyu soy sauce, similar to ceviche), <b>lomi lomi salmon</b>, <b>kalua pork</b> and <b>pork lau lau</b> (pork slow cooked in taro leaves) - served with two scoops of <b>rice</b> and one block of <b>haupia</b> (a coconut pudding-style desert).\n</p>\nThe whole thing cost about $7.50US!  I forget the name of the lunch place, but it was established in 1890.  <b>1890.</b>",
          "source": "commons-desc-page"
